HTTP Link Extractor

A Python script that extracts all HTTP and HTTPS links from a file and optionally downloads the files linked to by those URLs.

Features

* Extracts http:// and https:// links.
* Removes duplicate URLs.
* Lists all extracted links without downloading by default.
* Optionally downloads files from extracted URLs.
* Skips existing files when the destination filename already exists.
* Retries failed downloads up to three times.
* Supports a custom download directory.
* Streams downloads to reduce memory usage.

Requirements

* Python 3.9 or later
* requests

Installation

1. Create a Python virtual environment

A virtual environment keeps project dependencies separate from your system Python installation.

macOS / Linux

python3 -m venv .venv

Windows

python -m venv .venv

2. Activate the virtual environment

macOS / Linux

source .venv/bin/activate

Windows PowerShell

.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

Windows Command Prompt

.venv\Scripts\activate.bat

Once activated, your terminal should display (.venv).

3. Install dependencies

python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install requests

4. Deactivate the virtual environment

When you’re finished, run:

deactivate

You can reactivate the environment whenever you return to the project.

Usage

1. List all links

By default, the script only extracts and displays links. It does not download anything.

python workshop_links.py input.txt

Replace input.txt with the path to your input file.

2. Download all linked files

Pass the --download argument to download files from all extracted URLs.

python workshop_links.py input.txt --download

Downloaded files are saved in the workshop_downloads directory by default.

3. Specify an output directory

Use --output to choose a different download directory.

python workshop_links.py input.txt --download --output downloads

The output directory will be created automatically if it does not exist.

4. Save the extracted links to a text file

On macOS or Linux:

python workshop_links.py input.txt > links.txt

This captures the script’s console output, including status messages.

Command-Line Arguments

Argument	Required	Default	Description
file	Yes	—	Path to the input file
--download	No	Disabled	Download files from extracted URLs
--output	No	workshop_downloads	Directory where downloaded files are saved

How It Works

1. Reads the input file as UTF-8 text.
2. Searches for HTTP and HTTPS URLs.
3. Removes common trailing punctuation from extracted URLs.
4. Removes duplicate URLs while preserving their original order.
5. Prints the extracted URLs.
6. If --download is specified, downloads each URL into the output directory.
7. Retries failed downloads up to three times.

Important Notes

* Downloads are disabled by default. Files are downloaded only when --download is specified.
* The script is designed for text-based files. Binary files may require additional processing.
* Some URLs point to web pages rather than direct file downloads. These may download HTML instead of the intended resource.
* Different URLs may refer to files with the same filename. The script attempts to avoid overwriting existing files by adding an index to the filename.
* Only download files from sources you trust.

Project Structure

.
├── workshop_links.py
├── README.md
├── .gitignore
└── workshop_downloads/
    └── ...

Recommended .gitignore

To prevent the virtual environment and downloaded files from being committed to Git, add the following to .gitignore:

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
workshop_downloads/

